# .gitignore - special file for Git telling it which files to ignore when committing changes to the repository

# Ignore all data files except the one that's tracked
# Example: .csv
# Example: !sample-data.csv

# Ignore RStudio project files/folders
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# Ignore R cache and history
.RData
.RHistory
.Rhistory
.Ruserdata
.Rapp.history

# Ignore OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Ignore Logs
*.log
log.txt
logs.txt
logs/*
.coverage
*-lint-report*

# Ignore Editor cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Ignore AI coding tool configuration files, except AGENTS.md
.claude
.claude/*
.claudecode/*
.gemini
.gemini/*
.github-copilot
.github-copilot/*
.kimi
CLAUDECODE.md
GEMINI.md
KIMI.md
CHATGPT.md

# Ignore cache files
*.cache
__pycache__/
.venv/
# Build. Anchored: an unanchored `target` or `debug` would also ignore an app folder, a
# fixture, or a snapshot directory that happened to be named either of those.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
node_modules/
dist/

# Runtime data
/data/
/local/
/cache/
/identity/
# Anchored: the node's config.toml lives at the data root (spec/protocol.md §3), which is
# the repository root only in development. Unanchored, this also ignored
# `.cargo/config.toml` and would ignore any fixture or app manifest of that name.
/config.toml
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Lua
luac.out

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Secrets
*.key
*.pem
.env
# Except synthetic key material used by tests. spec/protocol.md §2.1 derives the node ID
# from the public key, so `test_spec_2_1_node_id_derivation` needs a fixed keypair
# checked in; without this it would be ignored silently and the test would look flaky.
!crates/*/tests/**/*.key
!crates/*/tests/**/*.pem

# Backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc with debugging information
*.pdb

# Cargo mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover JetBrains
.idea/
